---
title: 'Accessible Theme Test'
---

Every example on this page uses the `ag-accessible` theme. Toggle the website dark mode to check the same examples with `ag-accessible-dark`.

What to test, for every example:

- Confirm each series, or each item in a single-series chart, can be told apart by its pattern as well as its colour.
- Confirm text, axes and gridlines have enough contrast against the background in both light and dark mode.
- Tab into the chart and confirm the focus indicator is clearly visible.
- Confirm the legend items are large enough to be easy targets, and that toggling them works.

Additionally, for series with markers (line, area, range area, scatter, bubble, radar line and radar area):

- Confirm each series uses a different marker shape, and that markers have a solid fill rather than a pattern.

